<title>UK: P&amp;O European ferries see good Q1 growth.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O European ferries see good Q1 growth.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peninsular &amp; Oriental Steamship. Navigation Company Plc said on Wednesday its European ferries saw a significant increase in volume growth in the first quarter of the current year, while its cruise business made a strong start.</p>
<p>P&amp;O said, &quot;European ferries continued to achieve a significant increase in volume while Eurotunnel is not in full operation and that the total Short Sea market has seen further strong growth.&quot;</p>
<p>			 P&amp;O CRUISES</p>
<p>			Capacity Achieved (passenger berth days)</p>
<p>			 1st Quarter	   Year to date</p>
<p>			 1997	1996	1997	1996</p>
<p>Princess Cruises  930,739  1,017,238   930,739  1,017,238</p>
<p>P&amp;O Cruises (UK)  353,400   351,970    353,400   351,970</p>
<p>Load Factors (%)</p>
<p>			 1st Quarter		 Year to date</p>
<p>			 1997	1996	    1997	1996</p>
<p>Princess Cruises  100.0	99.6	    100.0     99.6</p>
<p>P&amp;O Cruises (UK)   92.2	92.9	     92.2     92.9</p>
<p>			P&amp;O EUROPEAN FERRIES</p>
<p>Short Sea Carryings (1)</p>
<p>			 1st Quarter		 Year to date</p>
<p>		     1997	1996	    1997	1996</p>
<p>Passengers     1,748,522 1,575,618     1,748,522 1,575,618</p>
<p>Tourist Vehicles 320,003   292,780	 320,003   292,780</p>
<p>Freight Units    159,819   103,726	 159,819   103,726</p>
<p>Total Carryings UK - Continent (2)</p>
<p>			 1st Quarter		 Year to date</p>
<p>		     1997	1996	    1997	1996</p>
<p>Passengers     2,222,555 2,047,510     2,222,555 2,047,510</p>
<p>Tourist Vehicles 410,652   377,630	 410,652   377,630</p>
<p>Freight Units    432,358   369,557	 432,358   369,557</p>
<p>P&amp;O said European Ferries Short Sea carryings were up by 9.3 percent for tourist vehicles and 54.1 percent for freight. The figures continued to be influenced by Eurotunnel's restricted operations.</p>
<p>The total Short Sea market for both tourist vehicles and freight continued to grow despite the reduction in Eurotunnel's capacity. Tourist vehicle carryings grew by 15.9 percent and freight by 6.4 percent.</p>
